      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Pharmacologic treatment and goal attainment rates from published literature indicate that lipid management has generally improved for patients with coronary heart disease. The population implications of these changes in lipid management are examined, suggesting that the challenge of lipid management may be shifting from a problem of no treatment to one of undertreatment."},
